NAME
       findfs - find a file system's device by label or UUID

SYNOPSIS
       findfs LABEL=NAME
       findfs UUID=UUID

DESCRIPTION
       findfs prints the device that holds the file system with that label or
       UUID, for example /dev/vdb1. It is a quick way to check what an
       /etc/fstab line written with LABEL= or UUID= points to. When nothing
       matches it says it is unable to resolve the name and exits with 1.

EXAMPLES
           findfs LABEL=BACKUP
           findfs UUID=3c1f6a0e-2b7d-4f0e-9d6a-1b2c3d4e5f60

SEE ALSO
       blkid(8), findmnt(8), fstab(5)
